# float simplify: rewrites of float instructions, each with a derivation
# (interval arithmetic in the float order, monotone preimages, the
# standard rounding model, the Vulkan precision table); no sampling
#
# a user's sRGB decode: no integer rewrites, but float ones
SAT simplify nofile
```glsl
vec3 decode(vec3 c) { return mix(c / 12.92, pow((c + 0.055) / 1.055, vec3(2.4)), step(vec3(0.04045), c)); }
```
# a color: c in [0, 1] bounds pow's base, so polynomial approximations
# are listed (cheaper, but beyond the precision pow already had)
simplify this shader with floats, c in [0, 1] nofile
```glsl
vec3 decode(vec3 c) { return mix(c / 12.92, pow((c + 0.055) / 1.055, vec3(2.4)), step(vec3(0.04045), c)); }
```
# bit-exact only: each rewrite differs somewhere (shown)
float simplify, bit-exact only, c in [0, 1] nofile
```glsl
vec3 decode(vec3 c) { return mix(c / 12.92, pow((c + 0.055) / 1.055, vec3(2.4)), step(vec3(0.04045), c)); }
```
# within 4 ulp of the reference: the select (0 ulp) and the fma (4 ulp)
simplify with floats, allow approximations within 4 ulp, c in [0, 1] nofile
```glsl
vec3 decode(vec3 c) { return mix(c / 12.92, pow((c + 0.055) / 1.055, vec3(2.4)), step(vec3(0.04045), c)); }
```
# a vec2: two lanes, one scalar function; sqrt is only used for v >= 0.25
# after the select, so x * inversesqrt(x) is defined there
float simplify nofile
```glsl
vec2 shade(vec2 v) { return mix(v * 2.0, sqrt(v), step(vec2(0.25), v)); }
```
# integer and float: SAT for the integer part, the float part after it
SAT simplify nofile
```glsl
float blend(uint n, float x) {
    uint m = (n * 4u) / 2u;
    return mix(x * 0.5, float(m & 255u), step(0.5, x));
}
```
# different constants per component: lanes x, y are bit-exact (powers of
# two), lane z fails where c + 0.3 cancels ...
simplify with floats, per component nofile
```glsl
vec3 tone(vec3 c) { return (c + vec3(0.1, 0.2, 0.3)) / vec3(2.0, 4.0, 1.5); }
```
# ... which c in [0, 1] excludes
simplify with floats, c in [0, 1] nofile
```glsl
vec3 tone(vec3 c) { return (c + vec3(0.1, 0.2, 0.3)) / vec3(2.0, 4.0, 1.5); }
```
# the polynomial approximations searched (approx's annealing over their
# f32 coefficients' ulps): what is found replaces the rounded fit's
# coefficients only when its certificate is better
simplify this shader with floats, c in [0, 1], search its polynomials by simulated annealing nofile
```glsl
vec3 decode(vec3 c) { return mix(c / 12.92, pow((c + 0.055) / 1.055, vec3(2.4)), step(vec3(0.04045), c)); }
```
